diff --git a/doc/src/sgml/libpq.sgml b/doc/src/sgml/libpq.sgml
index 68487a3954..b193dc4364 100644
--- a/doc/src/sgml/libpq.sgml
+++ b/doc/src/sgml/libpq.sgml
@@ -11401,4 +11401,38 @@ main(int argc, char **argv)
   </example>
 
  </sect1>
+ <sect1 id="libpq-borrowed-parameters">
+  <title>Experimental Borrowed Parameter Buffers</title>
+  <para>
+   <function>PQsendQueryParamsBorrowed</function> and
+   <function>PQsendQueryPreparedBorrowed</function> are experimental variants
+   of the corresponding asynchronous query functions. They accept an array of
+   <type>PQborrowedParam</type> structures in place of the value, length and
+   format arrays. Each parameter contains <structfield>segments</structfield>
+   (an array of <type>PQbuffer</type> pointer/length pairs),
+   <structfield>nsegments</structfield>, <structfield>format</structfield>
+   (zero for text or one for binary), and <structfield>isnull</structfield>
+   (zero or one). SQL NULL is distinct from a non-null zero-length parameter.
+   Text segments need no terminating zero and must not contain zero bytes.
+  </para>
+  <para>
+   Descriptor arrays are copied during the call. After a successful submission,
+   all referenced bytes must remain immutable and readable until
+   <function>PQflush</function> returns zero, or connection reset or
+   <function>PQfinish</function> returns. A negative flush result does not end
+   this obligation. Submission failure retains no new borrowed references;
+   a failure during transmission closes the transport. Flush completion does
+   not establish query success or commit success. Queries are never replayed.
+  </para>
+  <para>
+   These functions preserve the existing frontend/backend protocol. Plaintext
+   sockets can gather several segments in a single write. Encrypted transports
+   use their existing write functions with stable retry arguments; encryption
+   and operating-system buffering still apply. Protocol tracing uses the
+   ordinary copied parameter implementation. Existing query functions retain
+   their ownership contract, including when interleaved with borrowed queries
+   in pipeline mode. The feature macro is
+   <symbol>LIBPQ_HAS_BORROWED_PARAMS</symbol>.
+  </para>
+ </sect1>
 </chapter>
